Task: Hospital incidence regressions — Phase 2.

Summary: run_hospital_incidence.R + fit_incidence_dl() fit hospital-FE + year-FE
distributed-lag IRFs (Shock + Lag1 + Lag2 | CCN + Year, cluster State) for
{UncompCare_PctNPR, OperatingMargin, UncompCare_Real, NetMargin} x
{Is_Extreme_Drought, High_CDD, High_HDD, High_AQI_Max}; cumulative effect via
lincom(). Exports hospital_incidence_coefs.csv + IRF plots.

Findings: extreme drought lowers measured uncompensated care (%NPR and $);
High_HDD raises uncompensated $ (p=0.02); pooled margin effects insignificant
(heterogeneity is the Phase-4 story).

Files: Code/run_hospital_incidence.R, Code/tests/test_hospital_incidence.R.
Tests recover a known 2/1 DGP + cumulative=sum identity; all pass.
